  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1135 AM MDT Mon Jun 8 2026\n\nTriple digit temperatures make their presence felt today as a \nshortwave ridge is firmly in our region. Dewpoint temperatures in\nthe 30s and air temperatures in the upper 90s/lower 100s will keep\nrelative humidities for our area at or around 10%, so it will\nfeel very dry for the rest of the afternoon. Apart from some \nlingering high-level clouds, skies will be generally sunny.\n\nThe longwave trough off of New Mexico will deepen on Tuesday,\nbringing upper-level southerly flow into the high terrains. A\nthunderstorm or two is possible for the Sacramentos, but moisture\nlevels should remain relatively low.\n\nFor the rest of the week, the Borderland will be under a \nsubtropical high that is centered over South Texas and eventually \nmoves over the Chihuahuan Desert by the weekend. Temperatures will\nbe about 4-7 degrees above normal through Sunday. Lowland \nhotspots could reach 105 on Tuesday and/or Wednesday, so Heat \nAdvisories may be needed for the lowlands if the 105 degree \nthreshold is met.\n\nMoisture could make its much-needed return on Friday, but how west\nthe moisture will extend is still up to debate by the latest\nmodels runs. Any percentage of precipitaion for the weekend \nshould remain low until the models begin to align.",
